  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The Sankey diagram shows the energy flow in a car.  </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>Which one of the following statements is <strong>incorrect</strong> for the diagram?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">More than 80% of the energy losses are in the form of heat loss.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">The efficiency of the engine is 25%.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">The ratio of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Useful  energy}{Heat  loss  in  engine}\"></span> = <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">Over half of the total energy is lost in the engine. </li>\n</ol>"
  },
